  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to be crowded; to be packed; to be congested",
      "explanation": "Describes a place being full of people, making it difficult to move around. Used for trains, shops, roads, and other spaces."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "21395_komiau_ex1",
      "japanese": "{電車|でんしゃ}が{込|こ}み{合|あ}っている。",
      "english": "The train is crowded.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "21395_komiau_ex2",
      "japanese": "{年末|ねんまつ}は{空港|くうこう}がとても{込|こ}み{合|あ}う。",
      "english": "The airport gets very crowded at the end of the year.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "21395_komiau_ex3",
      "japanese": "{昼|ひる}どきのレストランは{込|こ}み{合|あ}っていて、{三十分|さんじゅっぷん}も{待|ま}たされた。",
      "english": "The restaurant was packed at lunchtime, and I had to wait thirty minutes.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Describes places being crowded with people. Most commonly used in the ている form ({込|こ}み{合|あ}っている) to describe the current state of congestion. Also written as {混|こ}み{合|あ}う, but the {込|こ}み{合|あ}う spelling is also standard.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {道|みち}が{込|こ}み{合|あ}う: the road is congested\n- {店|みせ}が{込|こ}み{合|あ}う: the shop is crowded\n- {窓口|まどぐち}が{込|こ}み{合|あ}う: the counter is busy\n- {込|こ}み{合|あ}う{時間帯|じかんたい}: peak hours\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {混雑|こんざつ}する: to be congested — more formal, used in announcements and signage\n- {混|こ}む: to be crowded — simpler form with the same basic meaning; {込|こ}み{合|あ}う emphasizes greater intensity\n- {賑|にぎ}わう: to be bustling — implies liveliness and positive energy, not just density of people",
  "schema_version": "2.0",
